cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use denote in research or teaching, please cite it as below."
title: "denote: a type-driven workbench for compositional model-theoretic semantics"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-07
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "denote contributors"
abstract: >-
  denote composes sentence meanings from typed lambda-term lexicons and constituency trees,
  derives scope readings by four mechanisms (QR, Cooper storage, continuations, flexible types),
  computes presupposition projection under three trivalent schemes, tests generalized-quantifier
  universals, and reports model-theoretic statistics over finite model classes.
keywords: [formal semantics, lambda calculus, compositionality, quantifier scope, presupposition]
